  "annotation": {
    "schema_version": 5,
    "type": "new architecture support",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "Gemma3ForConditionalGeneration was not registered. Its nested text configuration and alternating local/global attention require architecture-specific assembly.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_d7be3529fb7044769f9d5c2cdb41fb37",
          "call_a308eb9de1684b5b9773c3cc7fcace34",
          "call_fc0157278e8c4f0a9d731cd00d27d144"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "The change reuses existing transformer modules and extends the RoPE configuration helper to accept a separate dictionary and caller-specific defaults. This permits globally scaled RoPE and independent, unscaled local RoPE without changing the previous helper defaults.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_4a342866b5dd4a02906ef2cc832c1149",
          "call_a308eb9de1684b5b9773c3cc7fcace34",
          "call_1ba8c576e4244387bde5150872b02799"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "Directory-based dispatch can now select Gemma3's text model. Vision is represented separately, but its load and unload methods explicitly raise NotImplementedError; this is not multimodal inference support.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_562ade57beef4a6f953d5fac5033c368",
          "call_db35e6b199614f8ea7d3333427b22e58",
          "call_d7be3529fb7044769f9d5c2cdb41fb37",
          "call_a308eb9de1684b5b9773c3cc7fcace34"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "source_notes": [
      {
        "text": "The preceding entry describes the component dictionary and additional-tensor compilation hook that this adapter uses.",
        "basis": "ancestor",
        "evidence": [
          "call_a7a30ffe1a2d402f8464a76fc7d2a910"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "PR #4, \u201cchore: update config.py,\u201d proposes a spelling correction. Issue #7, \u201cquantizing model: undefined symbol: __cxa_call_terminate,\u201d reports extension loading failure; issue #6, \u201cNo ROCm runtime is found, using ROCM_HOME='/usr',\u201d reports a build-time assertion. Their connection to this change is inferred only from the shared config.py path and matching RoPE import traceback, not evidence that this architecture addition fixes them.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_96b66b0a197944e1a03f5837d2ef0bbf",
          "call_8b7d7c4324ff4daf950b304a9e8640b9",
          "call_ad3377f5a8c243b295503940e9952f56",
          "call_562ade57beef4a6f953d5fac5033c368"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Issue #29, \u201cAuto-YaRN for Qwen3? Maybe even set it dynamically?\u201d, discusses request-dependent scaling and its cache/batching complications. Its relationship here is inferred from shared RopeSettings and rope.py references; Gemma3's two fixed settings do not implement that proposal.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_75594ade985c4279b3c2bbf1d591e3e9",
          "call_a308eb9de1684b5b9773c3cc7fcace34"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "No model loading, generation, conversion or GPU execution was performed. Configuration agreement does not establish tensor-layout compatibility or numerical correctness.",
      "The Python computation transcribed layer scheduling and attention-scale arithmetic; it did not execute the model or attention kernels.",
      "Model configurations were supplied as hash-verified historical mirror files. Omitted configuration values establish which adapter defaults apply, not independent validation of those defaults."
    ],
    "links": [
      "830b6a018070a327d6d261628dff496f1303cf93"
    ],
    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "models",
        "title": "Gemma3 text assembly and separate positional settings",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "Gemma3Config registers Gemma3ForConditionalGeneration and supplies text and vision component classes. The existing factory defaults to text. Configuration reads dimensions from text_config, requires num_hidden_layers, and supplies vocabulary size 262208 when the base configuration finds neither top-level nor nested vocab_size.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_a308eb9de1684b5b9773c3cc7fcace34",
              "call_562ade57beef4a6f953d5fac5033c368",
              "call_db35e6b199614f8ea7d3333427b22e58"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "read_rope_settings_default now distinguishes an omitted dictionary from an explicitly empty one. Global settings read text_config with theta defaulting to 1,000,000; local settings read {}, yielding theta 10,000, full rotary dimensions and no scaling. Both use NEOX layout. Existing calls that supply only rope_style retain top-level configuration and the previous defaults.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_4a342866b5dd4a02906ef2cc832c1149",
              "call_a308eb9de1684b5b9773c3cc7fcace34",
              "call_edf1a0b2c34e4d6d9ac284d82b92c461"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Layer locality is bool((idx + 1) % sliding_window_pattern): with the default period 6, every sixth layer is global. Local layers receive the configured sliding_window, while global layers receive -1. The adapter's fallback window is 4096, but every inspected model explicitly supplies 1024. FlashAttention consumers forward the window and query_pre_attn_scalar**(-0.5); the SDPA path explicitly rejects sliding-window attention.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_a308eb9de1684b5b9773c3cc7fcace34",
              "call_f8357c9e9daf4439afda25ce234c453f",
              "call_251ef966e09540a9ba0a600bc2eafe72"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The inspected RoPE implementation computes inverse frequencies from theta and rotary dimension. Linear scaling divides them by the configured factor. Consequently the inspected checkpoints' factor 8 applies to global attention only; the empty local dictionary deliberately bypasses it.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_1ba8c576e4244387bde5150872b02799",
              "call_a308eb9de1684b5b9773c3cc7fcace34",
              "call_ecb6693a84564e20b0b235f545bd8667"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Text tensor keys retain the language_model prefix. Assembly comprises a normalized embedding, sequential attention and GELU-gated MLP residual branches with pre/post RMSNorm, a final half-precision norm, and a vocabulary projection with the embedding key as an alternative. Q and K receive RMSNorm before RoPE. Norms use constant_bias=1; branch post-norms request float output.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_a308eb9de1684b5b9773c3cc7fcace34",
              "call_2b1721e94dc84799b91750c1d1cfc3b7",
              "call_f8357c9e9daf4439afda25ce234c453f"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "google/gemma-3-4b-it and google/gemma-3-4b-pt each map to hidden/intermediate widths 2560/10240 and 34 layers, overriding the adapter's width defaults. Both omit head counts and head_dim, so the adapter supplies 8 query heads, 4 KV heads and dimension 256. google/gemma-3-4b-it-qat-int4-unquantized and google/gemma-3-4b-it-qat-q4_0-unquantized explicitly supply those same dimensions, counts and query scalar 256.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_ecb6693a84564e20b0b235f545bd8667",
              "call_bda781bf93704452a8f796745c57ac17",
              "call_1ebe29c11667467a97b76e4908137c57",
              "call_d8c518950237414da8a906815134dbbc",
              "call_a308eb9de1684b5b9773c3cc7fcace34"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "google/gemma-3-12b-it and google/gemma-3-12b-pt each supply widths 3840/15360, 48 layers and 16/8 query/KV heads; the adapter supplies omitted head_dim and query scalar as 256. google/gemma-3-12b-it-qat-int4-unquantized and google/gemma-3-12b-it-qat-q4_0-unquantized explicitly confirm those dimensions and scalar. Thus none of these four uses the adapter's default widths or head counts.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_645d5d5f1f3642338809235d6a27712d",
              "call_7c26c059040c4785b91a3e9bae0f67eb",
              "call_92052473970a4ffba44b75b92fa0e7e2",
              "call_3647a2df32f84e6aaac7b29490a2b4e9",
              "call_a308eb9de1684b5b9773c3cc7fcace34"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "google/gemma-3-27b-it, google/gemma-3-27b-pt and google/gemma-3-27b-it-qat-q4_0-unquantized each supply widths 5376/21504, 62 layers, 32/16 query/KV heads, head_dim 128 and query scalar 168. The adapter reads these overrides rather than deriving the attention scale from head_dim.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_6e714ddc05184d71a0a2f519fb24ff2d",
              "call_2ce5fa2a843447a4b824017e7437432d",
              "call_46fe15e33a254bbbaae9e7098d7e5e24",
              "call_a308eb9de1684b5b9773c3cc7fcace34"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "All eleven inspected configurations use the registered architecture and nested text_config, with linear RoPE factor 8 and window 1024. The five QAT configurations explicitly specify period 6, theta 1,000,000, local base frequency 10,000 and vocabulary 262208. Their null attention/output softcaps fall through read_dict to the adapter's 0.0 defaults. Local base frequency is not read by this adapter, but its fixed 10,000 agrees with those files.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_a308eb9de1684b5b9773c3cc7fcace34",
              "call_51da57dbe0e54d518eb83754702729cf",
              "call_1ebe29c11667467a97b76e4908137c57",
              "call_d8c518950237414da8a906815134dbbc",
              "call_92052473970a4ffba44b75b92fa0e7e2",
              "call_3647a2df32f84e6aaac7b29490a2b4e9",
              "call_46fe15e33a254bbbaae9e7098d7e5e24",
              "call_ecb6693a84564e20b0b235f545bd8667",
              "call_bda781bf93704452a8f796745c57ac17",
              "call_645d5d5f1f3642338809235d6a27712d",
              "call_7c26c059040c4785b91a3e9bae0f67eb",
              "call_6e714ddc05184d71a0a2f519fb24ff2d",
              "call_2ce5fa2a843447a4b824017e7437432d"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A bounded Python transcription produced local/global layer counts of 29/5, 40/8 and 52/10 for 34, 48 and 62 layers. The corresponding query scales are 0.0625 for scalar 256 and approximately 0.077151675 for scalar 168. These are schedule and scalar checks, not model execution.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_2483a2d4a92f4a0f97880f7f6cd435ee"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The vision class's additional-tensor hook returns the union of source entries under vision_tower and multi_modal_projector. This preserves a separation between text execution and additional checkpoint tensors without implementing a vision forward path.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_a308eb9de1684b5b9773c3cc7fcace34"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "findings": [],
    "summary": "Adds Gemma3 text-model dispatch and assembly with separate local/global RoPE settings; vision remains a stub with an additional-tensor hook."
  },
